# Day 11 - Introduction to Test Automation

## Objective
To understand the fundamentals of test automation, identify when automation should be used, learn different automation frameworks and tools, 
and set up the Selenium automation environment using Java.

---

## Tools Used
- Java JDK 21
- Eclipse IDE
- Selenium WebDriver
- Maven
- Google Chrome
- ChromeDriver

---

## Topics Covered

### 1. Test Automation Fundamentals
Learned:
- What is Test Automation
- Benefits of Automation Testing
- Challenges of Automation
- Return on Investment (ROI)

---

### 2. When to Automate
Understood suitable automation scenarios:

**Recommended**
- Regression Testing
- Smoke Testing
- Stable Features
- Data-Driven Testing

**Not Recommended**
- Exploratory Testing
- Frequently Changing UI
- One-Time Testing
- Usability Testing

---

### 3. Automation Tools Overview
Explored commonly used automation tools:
- Selenium (Web Automation)
- Appium (Mobile Automation)
- Cypress (Modern Web Testing)
- Playwright (Cross-Browser Testing)
- JUnit / TestNG (Testing Frameworks)
- Postman / REST Assured (API Testing)

---

### 4. Automation Frameworks
Learned different automation framework types:
- Data-Driven Framework
- Keyword-Driven Framework
- Hybrid Framework
- Page Object Model (POM)

Also understood the purpose and advantages of each framework.

---

### 5. Automation Environment Setup
Configured the Selenium Java automation environment:
- Verified Java JDK installation
- Installed Eclipse IDE
- Created Maven project
- Added Selenium WebDriver dependency
- Configured Chrome browser
- Executed first Selenium project

---

### 6. First Selenium Automation Script
Created and executed a basic Selenium script to:
- Launch Chrome browser
- Navigate to a website
- Locate a web element
- Perform an action
- Verify the result
- Close the browser

---

### 7. Test Automation Pyramid
Learned the automation testing pyramid:
- Unit Testing
- Integration Testing
- End-to-End (E2E) Testing

Also understood why automation should focus more on lower testing levels.

---

## Deliverables Completed
- Automation environment setup completed
- First Selenium automation script executed
- Automation tools comparison documented
- When to Automate checklist prepared
- Automation strategy document created
- README with automation basics completed

---

## Conclusion
Day 11 introduced the fundamentals of test automation, automation frameworks, and Selenium WebDriver. 
It also involved setting up the Java Selenium environment and executing the first automation script, providing a strong foundation for advanced Selenium concepts.
